<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estanislao Figueras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1819">1819</a>–<a href="/years/1882">1882</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Estanislao Figueras was a Catalan lawyer and republican politician who became the first President of the Executive Power of the First Spanish Republic when it was proclaimed in February 1873 after Amadeo I abdicated. Overwhelmed by divisions between federal and unitary republicans, the Carlist war and unrest, he left office abruptly in June 1873 and was succeeded by Francesc Pi i Margall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estanislao-figueras.jpg" alt="Estanislao Figueras" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arturo Carretero · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Estanislao_Figueras.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
